message:
Reimplement check with a blacklist of modules and a reduce

Check any calls following Map.get for membership in
@unsafe_modules.  Also implement new test.

Allow regexes in lint attributes

This provides a way to e.g. deactivate all Refactor checks:

    @lint [{~r/Refactor/, false}]

Declare var/0 as built-in type (#8286)

Redefining the pseudo-type "var" might lead to ambiguous typespecs.

Here is an example:

    defmodule DefineVarType do
      @type my_var :: integer
      @type var :: integer

      @spec foo(x, x, var) :: boolean when x: var
      def foo(x, y, z), do: x + y == z

      @spec bar(x, x, my_var) :: boolean when x: my_var
      def bar(x, y, z), do: x + y == z
    end

Add number of skipped tests to ExUnit output

- Skipped tests now count toward the total
- Include number of skipped tests in runner return
value:

Before: %{failures: 0, total: 3}
After:  %{failures: 0, skipped: 1, total: 3}

Do not add spaces after { and before }

This makes the source code consistent with the result
returned by inspect/2.

Change typespec guards to keyword list

Previous syntax:
@spec fun(a) :: b when is_var(a) and is_subtype(b, [a])
New syntax:
@spec fun(a) :: b when a: var, b: [a]

Refactor Koan with slow/fast process example

A combined solution of the examples provided by
@iamvery and myself.

Accept binaries for ttl parameters (#265)

* also accept binaries for ttl, ie: {"5", :days} and {5, :days}

* accept binaries for both ttl number and period, ie: {"5", "days"} and {5, :days}

Make sure sockets with unconfigured endpoints raise warning (#2459)

This brings sockets in line with how connections and raw endpoints are treated
by Phoenix.Token.{sign,verify}
